Optimal Solution - Count frequencies using HashMap and return the largest number whose value equals its occurrence.
                  “Since we need frequency comparison, I use a HashMap to count occurrences and then check which number equals its count.”

class Solution {
    public int findLucky(int[] arr) {
        // Map to store frequency of each number
        HashMap<Integer, Integer> map = new HashMap<>();
        // Count frequency of each element
        for (int num : arr) {
            map.put(num, map.getOrDefault(num, 0) + 1);
        }
        int max = -1;  // Stores largest lucky number
        // Traverse through all unique numbers
        for (int key : map.keySet()) {
            // If number equals its frequency → lucky number
            if (key == map.get(key)) {
                // Keep the maximum lucky number
                max = Math.max(max, key);
            }
        }        
        // Return largest lucky number or -1 if none exists
        return max;
    }
}

Time Complexity :- O(N).
Space Complexity :- O(N).
